## Program Constraints

- Normal scenarios use guarded public lifecycle/reporting services and retain completed history;
  cleanup cannot manufacture a passing clean tail.
- Independent read-only inspection owns the oracle. Narrow time, interruption, and corruption
  hooks fail closed outside verified development fixtures.
- Live reporter identity, sequence, credential, and hosted cursor state are never partially reset
  or borrowed for destructive tests.
- Existing-instance snapshots are sanitized without changing structural identities, revisions,
  lineage, verdicts, reconciliation, or representative lifecycle shape. Until M4 passes, their
  hosted intake is confined to a dedicated ephemeral development database and excluded from the
  shared operational development inventory.
- Recoverable parent projections are rebuilt from authoritative content. Missing parent authority
  remains an explicit unresolved-ancestor blocker that holds its chain open; the system never
  fabricates completion or leaves an invisible orphan.
- Required unknown, stale, missing, conflicting, or unavailable state prevents `PASS`.
- Correctness precedes timing. Larger absolute ceilings and any budget revision require retained
  measurements from the same platform and target class.
- Work2 modifies development lanes only. Work3 freezes and qualifies; Work5 production promotion
  remains a separate explicit request.

## Verification Strategy

- Compare canonical local facts, an independently calculated graph, stored rollups, outbox and
  sequence records, hosted base/projection rows, HTTP/view-model values, and bounded browser-visible
  claims at each declared checkpoint.
- For QH-010, seal an exact pre-upgrade source inventory, then compare exact local and hosted sets
  after upgrade, first ingestion, interruption/resume, duplicate delivery, reordered delivery, and
  idempotent replay.
- Assert exact values, set equality, cardinality, monotonic revisions, bounded convergence, required
  presence, and zero unexpected rows.
- Preserve the original replay and any minimized replay with candidate, fixture, platform,
  scenario, seed, action order, failure signature, hashes, and evidence locations.
- Keep `PASS`, `PRODUCT-FAIL`, `HARNESS-FAIL`, and `INFRA-BLOCKED` distinct; only complete required
  cross-platform observations may satisfy a gate.

